<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3261] AffinityKey is not stored in the metadata cache</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3261</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Presently we don&apos;t register predefined and system classes in metadata cache which can lead to significant performance drops when these types used as keys.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As an example we have &lt;tt&gt;AffinityKey&lt;/tt&gt; class. It&apos;s not registered in the metadata cache and as a result client nodes don&apos;t update their &lt;tt&gt;CacheObjectBinaryProcessorImpl.clientMetaDataCache&lt;/tt&gt;. After that when a client node needs to get &lt;tt&gt;AffinityKey&lt;/tt&gt; metadata using &lt;tt&gt;CacheObjectBinaryProcessorImpl.metadata(typeId)&lt;/tt&gt; it will always call metadata cache and this is a bottleneck. The drop can be significant because this method is called from methods like &lt;tt&gt;GridAffinityProcessor.mapKeyToPrimaryAndBackups&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In attach you can find a simple benchmark that shows how slower a result if AffinityKey is used.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a solution we can register &lt;tt&gt;AffinityKey&lt;/tt&gt; and other system and predefined classes &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/help_16.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt; in the metadata cache.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
